      "dcterms:title": "Strongly coupled quantum discrete Liouville theory I: algebraic approach and duality",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "APPROACH, THEORY. I: ALGEBRAIC",
        "DUALITY"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20181022",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0006156",
      "dcterms:abstract": "The quantum discrete Liouville model in the strongly cou- pled regime, 1 < c < 25, is formulated as a well deﬁned quantum me- chanical problem with unitary evolution operator. The theory is self- dual: there are two exponential ﬁelds related by Hermitean conjugation, satisfying two discrete quantum Liouville equations, and living in mu- tually commuting subalgebras of the quantum algebra of observables.",
